  "coverage": [
    "CUDA base/quadratic/cubic challenge powers, lookup prefixes and mapped challenge pairs, and next-row points match independent CPU field calculations, including noncanonical inputs and zero values.",
    "Power exponents cover zero, nonzero and u64::MAX, with checked exponent addition. Lookup tuple widths cover 1, 7, 33 and u32::MAX; counts cover the 4096-output boundary.",
    "Split domains up to 256 cosets and disjoint shifts through log-size 32 match upstream TwoAdicMultiplicativeCoset. CUDA owns the resulting shift buffers; no intermediate host field arithmetic or readback is required.",
    "Whole-operation admission rejects bad spans, widths, counts, domains, IDs, insufficient allocation size, and exhausted aggregate storage before issuing arithmetic or consuming transcript samples.",
    "The CUDA lookup adapter preserves shared global bus names, distinct local buses, empty instances and maximum-size batches; its only upload is the public bus-ID mapping. It samples the original alpha/beta pair directly to device memory.",
    "Upstream BatchTranscript and LogUpGadget independently match every per-instance challenge pair and the following transcript sample; empty lookups consume nothing.",
    "A resident stage chain derives lookup challenges, samples the quotient alpha, evaluates a specialized cubic quotient and commits its result. The only upload is one public bus ID; the only download before the final audit is the eight-byte quotient-domain status.",
    "The stage-chain quotient values and Merkle root match independent CPU arithmetic and hashing. This is not a complete proof.",
    "Scalar failure or unwind after CUDA execution retires related transcript snapshots; separate attempts remain usable. Memory-limit rejection in the lookup adapter occurs before sampling.",
    "OpenCL reuses the same bounded bus-index mapping and DomainSpec metadata. Arithmetic, lookup adapter and quotient regressions pass.",
    "Three streaming host tests preserve exact allocation accounting: the 4096-entry lookup mapping requests 229376 bytes, and excess empty instances are rejected before metadata allocation.",
    "CPU-only, OpenCL, Apple Metal cross-compilation and standalone CUDA builds pass. NVRTC compiles scalar kernels for compute_70 and compute_120; only sm_120 executes locally."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Full wallet and recursive proofs are not routed through CUDA; default proof/backend selection is unchanged.",
    "Randomness/hiding, witness/preprocessing/lookup evaluation, openings/FRI/final-polynomial work, complete PCS/backend selection, stage receipts, controller admission and pool integration remain incomplete.",
    "The new lookup adapter returns resident pairs and bounded instance ranges; complete native lookup trace construction and per-instance PCS integration remain future work.",
    "Resource limits here belong to the native runtime and bounded test services. Existing OpenCL worker assignments do not qualify CUDA worker admission.",
    "No V100 execution, Metal execution or full-proof performance/transaction-throughput claim is established."
  ],
